{"name":"Woollen Mittens","hex":"#b59f55","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woollen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of woolen."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of woolen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woollen"},{"term":"mittens","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of mitten"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of mitten"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mittens"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woolen","blocks":[{"text":"Woolen or woollen is a type of yarn made from carded wool. Woolen yarn is soft, light, stretchy, and full of air. It is thus a good insulator, and makes a good knitting yarn. Woolen yarn is in contrast to worsted yarn, in which the fibers are combed to lie parallel rather than carded, producing a hard, strong yarn."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woolen","wikidata":"Q1751888"},{"title":"Mitten","blocks":[{"text":"A mitten is a type of glove that covers the hand but does not have separate finger openings or sheaths. Generally, mittens still separate the thumb from the other four fingers. They have different colours and designs. Mittens provide greater thermal insulation than gloves as they have a smaller surface area exposed to the cold, but have a trade-off in dexterity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Southern_Sami_Mittens_Norway.JPG/330px-Southern_Sami_Mittens_Norway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitten","wikidata":"Q1661108"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Fold_mitten_Klappf%C3%A4ustling_2_in_1_Handschuh_07.JPG/500px-Fold_mitten_Klappf%C3%A4ustling_2_in_1_Handschuh_07.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Fo